            "ontology_mapping": {
              "evidence": [
                {
                  "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                  "notes": "[HISTORICAL \u2014 superseded by the #321 re-grade below: this record is a hydrate of CHEBI:35696, not an exact match to it] Imported from CultureMech pipeline, quality=DIRECT_MATCH",
                  "source": "CultureMech"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                  "notes": "identifier CHEBI:35696 -> kgmicrobe.compound:cocl2_x_2_h2o; mapping_quality EXACT_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is a hydrate of CHEBI:35696 ('cobalt dichloride') and was sharing that term's identifier \u2014 the identity collapse MAPPING_SEMANTICS \u00a73 forbids, which made a distinct substance indistinguishable from its anhydrous parent downstream. ChEBI has no term for this hydrate and the record carries no verified CAS, so steps 1 and 2 are unavailable and step 3 applies.",
                  "source": "MIM curation (#321/#334)"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                  "notes": "molecular_formula '2Cl.Co' -> '2Cl.Co.2H2O'. The recorded value described the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by 18 g/mol per water. Corrected because the label states 2 water(s) of hydration, and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:35696's ChEBI formula ('2Cl.Co') \u2014 the mark of a value inherited from the parent rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated notation.",
                  "source": "MIM curation (#321)"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                  "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:35696 ('cobalt dichloride') \u2014 a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged.",
                  "source": "MIM curation (#342)"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
                  "notes": "MediaDive578 and five current source recipes name CoCl2\u00b72H2O; publisher-deposited primary abstract reports single-crystal CoCl2\u00b72H2O. Retain the local two-water identity, without selecting an unverified CAS lead. No exact eligible term was established by bounded queries. CHEBI35696 is the closest verified water-free parent; use NARROW_MATCH/broadMatch and retain exact local identity. Current2Cl.Co.2H2O matches the source-defined stoichiometry. Dry structure fields were removed in7b and remain absent. Computed PubChem is corroboration, not the sole experimental proof. Primary source references: https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1063/1.1726454; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/cid/129656378/property/Title,MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,CanonicalSMILES/JSON; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/35696/. Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json. This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner bytes withdraw inherited support.",
                  "source": "MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)"
                }
              ],
